# UI / Design System Rules (`packages/ui/*`)

## Tailwind v4 — CSS-first

- Design tokens (colors, spacing, fonts, radii) live in the shared
  `@theme` block in `packages/ui/theme.css`. Never hardcode a hex color,
  arbitrary pixel value, or one-off font stack directly in a component
  file — add or reuse a token instead.
- There is no `tailwind.config.ts` to edit for tokens in this version —
  if you're about to create one for that purpose, stop and use `@theme` instead.

## Component conventions

- Every shared component exported from this package ships with a
  Storybook story exercising its prop variants (including loading/empty/
  error states where applicable) before it's imported into `apps/web`.
- Presentational only: no data fetching, no tRPC calls, no business logic
  inside `packages/ui`. Components receive data and callbacks as props.
- Built on shadcn/ui primitives where one exists for the pattern — don't
  hand-roll a dialog/dropdown/combobox that Radix/shadcn already provides
  correctly with accessibility handled.

## Domain-specific UI conventions (project-wide consistency)

- Monetary values always render as `PKR X,XXX,XXX` — use the shared
  `formatPKR()` helper, don't reimplement comma formatting inline.
- Status badges follow the fixed color mapping: green = verified/compliant,
  amber = pending, red = blocked/rejected, blue = informational/in-progress.
  Don't introduce a new ad-hoc color for a status — extend the shared
  `StatusBadge` variant set instead.
- CNIC display is always masked (`35202-XXXXX-X` pattern) outside of
  explicitly-gated admin/verification views — never render a full CNIC by default.

## Accessibility

- Every interactive element has a visible focus state and an accessible
  name (label, `aria-label`, or visually-hidden text) — this isn't optional
  polish, it's required before a component is considered done.
